  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are exempt from estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estates valued over ₱5,000,000, the estate tax liability will be calculated based on the net estate amount that exceeds this threshold. Executors or administrators of estates must ensure compliance with this tax obligation when filing the estate tax return, which is due within one year from the date of death of the decedent.",
